1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,323
We used to dare each other to ask Danny's uncle about his arm.

2
00:00:04,373 --> 00:00:06,482
He only ever said one thing.

3
00:00:06,532 --> 00:00:07,592
A wolf took it.

4
00:00:07,642 --> 00:00:08,825
On this street.

5
00:00:08,975 --> 00:00:10,607
We thought he was mad.

6
00:00:10,657 --> 00:00:12,567
Silver nails in the windowsill.

7
00:00:12,617 --> 00:00:14,717
Wolfsbane over the door.

8
00:00:14,767 --> 00:00:15,847
Every full moon,

9
00:00:15,897 --> 00:00:17,959
he sent us home before dark.

10
00:00:18,009 --> 00:00:21,021
Then he'd stand at the end of the road all night.

11
00:00:21,071 --> 00:00:22,654
Watching the houses.

12
00:00:22,804 --> 00:00:24,749
We called him Wolfman Mick.

13
00:00:25,139 --> 00:00:26,965
Mick died last week.

14
00:00:27,015 --> 00:00:28,650
I came home for the funeral.

15
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:30,592
Slept in my old room.

16
00:00:30,642 --> 00:00:32,807
First full moon in twenty years,

17
00:00:32,857 --> 00:00:35,203
with nobody at the end of the road.

18
00:00:35,673 --> 00:00:37,056
I woke at three.

19
00:00:37,106 --> 00:00:38,346
The window was open.

20
00:00:38,396 --> 00:00:39,917
Mud on the sill.

21
00:00:40,147 --> 00:00:41,881
Then Danny texted.

22
00:00:41,931 --> 00:00:45,046
Mum finally told me how Mick lost his arm.

23
00:00:45,096 --> 00:00:46,771
The summer we were ten.

24
00:00:46,821 --> 00:00:48,632
The night you went missing.

25
00:00:49,262 --> 00:00:51,117
I don't remember going missing.

26
00:00:51,267 --> 00:00:54,104
Mick wasn't watching for wolves getting in.

27
00:00:54,214 --> 00:00:56,552
He was watching for one getting out.

28
00:00:59,022 --> 00:00:59,997
Mick?
